       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1
1.1: Over 1,000 Small and Medium-sized Enterprises (SMEs) majority of which are led by women and youth have been equipped with knowledge, skills and tools to enable their participation in the AfCFTA market and they have also been facilitated to access markets in Democratic Republic of Congo, South Sudan and Rwanda through trade missions organized with the technical and financial support of UNDP. From the DRC trade mission alone, over 300 business to business deals were finalized to facilitate trade in chicken and chicken products, beef, milk, fruits, vegetables and cereals among others.(https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8AipweIBfbI; https://www.newvision.co.ug/category/news/ugandan-business-delegation-arrives-in-goma-a-135435)

